  "writeup": {
    "headline": "MSG Sports rates Hold: strong growth and price trend offset by very high absolute valuation.",
    "thesis": "MSG Sports scores 55, a Hold, because strong growth and trend are balanced by a weak valuation score of 12. Revenue was up 36.7% year on year in the latest quarter and up 11.0% on a trailing basis, with growth speeding up by 34.8 pp from the previous quarter. The shares are 15.0% above their 200-day average and up 79.8% from 12 months ago to 1 month ago, sitting 2.9% below their 52-week high. Valuation is high in absolute terms at 8.5x sales, 160.0x free cash flow and 342.7x EBIT, with the FCF yield 4.6 pp below the 10-year Treasury yield. Against its own history the stock is expensive overall (EV/EBIT not comparable): P/S is more expensive than at 53 of the last 61 month-ends, while P/FCF is near the middle of the last 61 month-ends. Thin margins (2.5% operating, 5.3% FCF) keep quality at 46, while the balance sheet scores a solid 69.",
    "key_risks": [
      "Very high absolute multiples (160.0x FCF, 342.7x EBIT) leave little room for disappointment.",
      "Thin operating margin of 2.5% means small cost or revenue shifts can swing profits.",
